diff --git a/docs/calculation-model.md b/docs/calculation-model.md
index f37f23d..e91483d 100644
--- a/docs/calculation-model.md
+++ b/docs/calculation-model.md
@@ -28,6 +28,14 @@ The deterministic keep policy protects held positive combo pieces and searches w
 
 Hidden top-deck banish and milling reduce deck capacity. Completed physical Exact also accounts for surviving target identities, including ordered draws, costs and removals. Banished-card and GY effects/recovery are not inferred. Fast may prove the same outcome exact, or require a certificate; do not infer accuracy merely from the presence of Desires or a draw effect.
 
+### Base Danger! reveal
+
+The nine Danger! monsters use the draw activation order. Each reveal discards one physical copy uniformly from the entire current hand, including the revealed copy. When the discard has the same canonical card identity, only the discarded copy leaves. Otherwise the revealed copy also leaves and one card is drawn. Surviving and newly drawn Danger! copies may activate again in the configured order. The reveal requires an available draw and a card in the deck.
+
+Matching uses the catalog identity across entries, even when the matching copy has its simulation disabled or its effect customized. The model covers the base reveal only. It omits separate discard-trigger effects and field or summon requirements.
+
+Fast can certify an interval when it counts only part of the physical discard and draw outcomes. Each lower endpoint counts resolved winning outcomes. The corresponding upper endpoint also includes the full unresolved probability mass. The UI shows the midpoint and rounds the uncertainty outward for each combo, group and total. When all outcomes resolve, both endpoints coincide.
+
 ## One excavation after draws
 
 After all draw effects, at most one held excavation source activates before ordinary searches. The eligible source with the highest excavation count wins; equal counts use stable entry identity, independent of visual deck order. Selection happens before revealing cards. Activation consumes the source even if no revealed target helps a combo; the model does not decline it, switch to another source, or excavate again after seeing the pool.
